<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal inflation rose to 0.2 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>Portugal inflation rose to 0.2 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese consumer prices rose 0.2 percent in November after -0.1 percent in October to give year-on-year inflation of 3.0 percent after 3.0 percent previously, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>Average annual inflation, the government's yardstick, was 3.1 percent in November after 3.2 percent previously.</p>
<p> PORTUGUESE INFLATION	  Nov 96	 Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p> Monthly CPI rise		  0.2	   -0.1	  0.1</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation		3.0	    3.0	  3.9</p>
<p> Average annual inflation	3.1	    3.2	  4.2</p>
<p> Index (base 100 1991)	 132.1	  131.9	128.6</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 3511-3538254</p>
</text>
